- op: discuss  # e5a8
  at: '2026-08-11T04:21:31Z'  # e5a8
  by: agent  # e5a8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e5a8
  clock: 4  # e5a8
  nonce: e5a8  # e5a8
  message: "PR #277 open and CI-green, raised with --gov so it will NOT auto-merge. Awaiting human merge (all five scripts are governance files).\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE from hypergumbo's own repro, both directions (legacy FORGEJO_* masked in .env, restored by a trap, values never printed):\n\n  BEFORE  $ ./scripts/ci-debug status  -> Error: FORGEJO_TOKEN not set...   exit 1\n          $ ./scripts/list-my-prs      -> Error: FORGEJO_TOKEN not set...   exit 1\n  AFTER   $ ./scripts/ci-debug status  -> 'Overall: success' + job list     exit 0\n          $ ./scripts/list-my-prs      -> 'No PRs found.'                   exit 0\n\nci-debug SUCCEEDING IS NOT PROOF THE TOKEN RESOLVED. This repo is public, so that call succeeds anonymously -- reading it as evidence of auth is exactly the error that hid the two-hour CI outage the day before. A separate probe pins the credential path itself: with FORGEJO_TOKEN masked empty, FORGE_BACKEND=github, FORGE_TOKEN non-empty and EQUAL to HG_GITHUB_TOKEN. That is the C9 path supplying the credential, not an anonymous read.\n\nCALL ORDER VERIFIED RATHER THAN ASSUMED: detect_api_base calls detect_forge_backend internally, and ci-debug/merge-pr/list-my-prs all run it before their guards, so a bare resolve_forge_token is correct at those three. auto-pr's two guards run BEFORE its detect_api_base, so they call detect_forge_backend explicitly. contribute resolves after detect_forge_backend \"$UPSTREAM_URL\" because its credential belongs to the upstream forge; its FORGEJO_USER guard stays (the fork-push credential helper uses it).\n\nUNPLANNED FINDING: the merge-pr close test replaces the WHOLE library with a hand-written stub, and that stub had drifted -- no resolve_forge_token, so bash exited 127 and five tests failed with assertions about PATCH bodies that named nothing about the cause. Stub now mirrors C9, and a new TestStubMirrorsTheRealLibrary asserts the stub defines every library function merge-pr actually calls; it immediately surfaced two more it lacked (do_merge_guarded, ci_verdict_permits_merge).\n\nTests: 187 passed. Status moves to satisfied only after the human merge, per closure-evidence discipline."  # e5a8
