  nonce: 41ea  # 41ea
  message: "SATISFIED. Human merged PR #277; merged dev is e9e1d8eb6a.\n\nCLOSURE EVIDENCE RE-RUN AGAINST MERGED dev (not just the feature branch), .env masked to HG_GITHUB_TOKEN only, restored by a trap, values never printed:\n  $ ./scripts/ci-debug status  -> 'CI status for commit e9e1d8eb / Overall: success' + job list, exit 0\n  $ ./scripts/list-my-prs      -> 'No PRs found.', exit 0\nAgainst the same masked env BEFORE the fix both exited 1 at the guard.\n\nAND THE CREDENTIAL-PATH PROBE, because this repo is PUBLIC and ci-debug therefore succeeds anonymously -- reading its success as proof of auth is the exact error that hid a two-hour CI outage. With FORGEJO_TOKEN masked empty: FORGE_BACKEND=github, FORGE_TOKEN non-empty and EQUAL to HG_GITHUB_TOKEN. So the guard passes because C9 resolved the PAT, not because of an unauthenticated read.\n\nPOSITIVE STRUCTURAL EVIDENCE that the invariant now holds, not just that the repro passes: zero occurrences of a direct credential read (TOKEN=\"${FORGEJO_TOKEN...}\") remain across auto-pr, ci-debug, merge-pr, contribute and list-my-prs. resolve_forge_token is called at all 8 former guard sites. Remaining FORGEJO_* references are error-message text, usage text, comments, and the FORGEJO_USER reads the fork-push credential helper legitimately needs.\n\nOPTIONAL FOLLOW-UP now unblocked (owner's call): the legacy FORGEJO_* values can be removed from .env permanently, since github is origin and the forgejo arm is dormant. Running the daily workflow with no FORGEJO_* values at all would be the strongest ongoing validation."  # 41ea
